      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8e45af67-e5bf-5148-9962-78f5c8cfbd3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Supergrass, Quietdrive\n- People: Mike Smith\n- Companies: EMI Publishing, Epic Records\n- Places: Oxford, Hopkins, Minnesota\n- Roles: Head of A&R\n- Products: Fall from the Ceiling EP\n- Topics: band formation, artist signing, music releases\n\nFacts:\n- Supergrass were an English rock band formed in 1993 in Oxford.\n- In 1992, Mike Smith moved to EMI Publishing and later became Head of A&R.\n- At EMI Publishing, Mike Smith signed acts including PJ Harvey, Elastica, Supergrass, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, The Scissor Sisters, The Arcade Fire, and Arctic Monkeys, and he re-signed Blur.\n- Quietdrive is an alternative rock band based in Hopkins, Minnesota that formed in 2002.\n- Quietdrive released the Fall from the Ceiling EP on September 27, 2005 under Epic Records.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b79b8fe1-7d1c-50fc-9256-620028047881",
        "text": "Page: Supergrass. Sentence: Supergrass were an English rock band, formed in 1993 in Oxford.\nPage: Quietdrive. Sentence: Quietdrive is an alternative rock band based in Hopkins, Minnesota that formed in 2002.\nPage: Mike Smith (A&amp;R man). Sentence: He then moved to EMI Publishing in 1992, where he went on to sign acts, such as PJ Harvey, Elastica, Supergrass, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, The Scissor Sisters, The Arcade Fire, and Arctic Monkeys, as well as resigning Blur and progressing to the position of Head of A&R.\nPage: Fall from the Ceiling. Sentence: Fall from the Ceiling EP by Quietdrive was released on September 27, 2005 under Epic Records.",
